grations.py`**: new migration `m027_turns_response_json` adds a nullable `turns.response_json` column.\n- **`llm/logs.py`**:\n  - Added the condensing helpers: `_payload_replacements`, `condense_payload`, `resolve_payload`, `_model_json_replacements`, and `TURN_TOOLS_SQL`.\n  - `log()` now stores the condensed payload on the turn.\n  - Added `LogStore.turn_response_json()` and `LogStore._turn_tool_pairs()`.\n  - `llm logs` rows now include `response_json`, resolved through `_LogRowBuilder._resolve_response_json`. A broken reference yields `None` instead of failing the listing.\n- **`llm/default_plugins/openai_models.py`**: in both `Responses` and `AsyncResponses` streaming, the reasoning done event is kept per item id. After the final payload arrives, `_reasoning_refresh_events` re-yields the final `encrypted_content` on the same part. The stored reasoning part therefore matches `response_json`, and the text is unchanged.\n\nTwo choices I made that the spec left open:\n- The sync and async `_reasoning_refresh_events` yields use `yield from` and a `for` loop respectively, as the spec asked. I wrote the two streaming edits with a split at `class AsyncResponses`, because the anchor text is identical in both classes.\n- I wrapped one long line in `log()` by hand. No formatter is installed in `.venv`, so the formatting is not checked by a tool.\n\n`SPEC.md` is still untracked in the worktree, and I did not commit anything.", "ttft_ms": 1108, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 221656, "uuid": "a2e34376-c727-42a8-8348-bb33865c6108", "ttft_stream_ms": 963, "time_to_request_ms": 231, "first_content_frame_ms": 963, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
